Use the **developer** subagent to build $ARGUMENTS in the native app ({{NATIVE_STACK}},
`{{APP_PACKAGE_ID}}`). Consume the VALIDATED screen spec + acceptance criteria from `{{STUDIO_REPO}}` and
COMPOSE `{{COMPONENT_LIB}}` — do not re-implement a component (a gap → `design-system-engineer`) or re-draw a
validated layout (the prototype is the spec; port native concerns, not pixels).

Run the `engineering_lens`: parity to the validated flow, state + data correctness (loading/empty/error/
success wired, async failures surface to the UI — never a silent dead tap), platform correctness (iOS +
Android build + behave, permissions honest, a11y carried from the components), performance (no needless
re-renders on the core loop, fonts preloaded), and device-verification of what only hardware proves.

Deliver: the engineering_lens result + the device-check status, and hand a verified build target to
`release-engineer` with the commit + what changed + what device checks remain. Defer to the agent — do not
restate the component API here.
